{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MarkovTraceAxiomaticClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MarkovTraceAxiomaticClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.RingDivision","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_degree_increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_degree_increasing","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L167-L189","doc":"The Hecke-power recurrence is degree-monotonic in the obvious\nsense for the leading-coefficient pattern.  Stated as:\n`degree(a_{k+2}) > degree(b_{k+1})` for k ≥ 0, by the explicit\nrecurrence and noting that `b_{k+1} = a_k`.\n\nThis is a structural fact used implicitly when reading off the\nclosed form: the leading degree of the proton expansion comes\nfrom the `a_7 · a_4 · z²` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB_four","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L162-L165","doc":"`b_4 = a_3 = h² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_four","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L155-L160","doc":"`a_4 = h³ + 2h` matches the hand computation\n`a_4 = h · a_3 + b_3 = h(h²+1) + h = h³ + 2h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB_three","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L150-L153","doc":"`b_3 = a_2 = h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_three","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L144-L148","doc":"`a_3 = h² + 1` matches the recurrence:\n`a_3 = h · a_2 + b_2 = h · h + 1 = h² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB_two","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L141-L142","doc":"`b_2 = 1` matches the hand computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA_two","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L135-L139","doc":"`a_2 = h` matches the hand computation\n`σ_i² = h σ_i + 1` ⇒ `a_2 = h, b_2 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePower_recurrence_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePower_recurrence_b","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L131-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePower_recurrence_a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePower_recurrence_a","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L126-L129","doc":"Sanity recurrences (smoke-tested, useful for downstream proofs). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTraceAxiomaticClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTraceAxiomaticClosedForm","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L78-L124","doc":"**Axiomatic closed form of the Markov trace for the proton word —\nexplicit coefficient polynomials.**\n\nThe closed form (`.md` sibling) reads\n\n  tr_M(σ_1^7 σ_2^4)(q) =\n    protonMarkovCoeffA · z²\n  + protonMarkovCoeffB · z\n  + protonMarkovCoeffC,\n\nwhere `protonMarkovCoeffA = a_7 a_4`, `protonMarkovCoeffB = a_7 b_4 +\nb_7 a_4`, `protonMarkovCoeffC = b_7 b_4` are the Hecke-power\ncoefficients (Laurent polynomials in `h = q - q⁻¹`) and\n`z = q³/(q² + 1)` (convention D).\n\nThe Hecke-power recurrence (`σ_i^k = a_k σ_i + b_k` with\n`a_{k+1} = h a_k + b_k`, `b_{k+1} = a_k`, derived by iterating the\nHecke quadratic `σ_i² = h σ_i + 1`) determines the three coefficient\npolynomials **exactly**.  This theorem discharges that exact\ndetermination: it states the closed polynomial form of the three\nproton coefficients in `h = X`,\n\n  A(h) = h^9 + 7h^7 + 16h^5 + 13h^3 + 2h,\n  B(h) = 2h^8 + 12h^6 + 22h^4 + 13h^2 + 1,\n  C(h) = h^7 + 5h^5 + 7h^3 + 3h,\n\nand is proved by unfolding the recurrence and `ring`.  The\nremaining `z`-assembly into the rational Markov trace\n(`A z² + B z + C`, denominator `q^7(q^2+1)^2` under the canonical\nconvention D) is the abstract\n`MarkovTrace`-typeclass step; the **content** the recurrence\nmachinery actually establishes — the three coefficient polynomials\n— is what this theorem fixes, mirroring the symbolic\n`markov_trace_atomic_proton_full.py` witness.\n\nRef: [jones1987] §5; [kassel1995] Theorem III.3.3. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form","label":"prop:markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonMarkovCoeffC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonMarkovCoeffC","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonMarkovCoeffB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonMarkovCoeffB","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L74-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.protonMarkovCoeffA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.protonMarkovCoeffA","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L65-L73","doc":"Closed-symbol form of the proton Markov trace.\n\nReads `tr_M(σ_1^7 σ_2^4) = A z² + B z + C` with\n   A = a_7 · a_4,\n   B = a_7 · b_4 + b_7 · a_4,\n   C = b_7 · b_4,\nwhere `(a_k, b_k)` are the Hecke-power coefficients in\n`h = q - q⁻¹`, evaluated below at the formal Laurent variables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerB","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L59-L63","doc":"Hecke-power coefficient `b_k(h)` defined by the recurrence\n`b_{k+1} = a_k`, `b_0 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckePowerA","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/markov-trace-axiomatic-closed-form.lean#L50-L57","doc":"Hecke-power coefficient `a_k(h)` defined by the recurrence\n`a_{k+1} = h · a_k + b_k`, `a_0 = 0`, `a_1 = 1`.  Since `b_{k+1} = a_k`\n(see `heckePowerB`), the mutual recurrence collapses to the two-term\n`a_{k+2} = X · a_{k+1} + a_k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}